-- title:
--   Closed subalgebras as pro-Artinian objects; trace algebra object
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathcal O$ is a commutative local ring and $A$ an object of `ProartinianCat 𝓞`, i.e. a topological $\mathcal O$-algebra that is local, pro-Artinian (linearly topologised with a basis of open ideals, $T_0$, complete, and with $A/I$ Artinian for every open ideal $I$), whose structure map reflects units, and whose residue field is reached by $\mathcal O$. Two preliminary facts are recorded: for $m\in\mathfrak m_A$ the powers $m^N$ tend to $0$ (every open ideal contains a power of $\mathfrak m_A$); and, for $A$ compact, if $T\subseteq A$ is closed and contains all partial geometric sums $\sum_{i<N}m^i$ with $m\in\mathfrak m_A$, then some $s\in T$ satisfies $s(1-m)=1$. From these comes the unit-detection lemma `isUnit_of_isUnit_val`: if $S\subseteq A$ is a closed $\mathcal O$-subalgebra, $A$ is compact and $x\in S$ has unit image in $A$, then $x$ is a unit of $S$ (write $x\cdot\mathrm{alg}(o^{-1})=1-m$ with $m\in\mathfrak m_A\cap S$ and sum the geometric series inside the closed set $S$).
--
--   The `ClosedSubalgebra` group then establishes, for closed $S\subseteq A$ with $A$ compact, each clause of the ambient structure: $S$ is nontrivial and local, $x\in\mathfrak m_S$ iff $x\in\mathfrak m_A$, $\mathcal O\to S$ reflects units, $\mathcal O$ surjects onto the residue field of $S$, the subspace topology is a ring topology with basis of neighbourhoods of $0$ the contractions $I\cap S$ of open ideals $I\subseteq A$ (hence linear), $S$ is compact and pro-Artinian (quotients by open ideals are finite), and so $S$ carries `IsLocalProartinianAlgebra 𝓞 S`. Consequently `closedSubalgebraObj S hS` is the object of `ProartinianCat 𝓞` with carrier $S$, and `closedSubalgebraι S hS` the morphism given by the inclusion, which sends $x$ to its underlying element of $A$ and is injective.
--
--   Finally, assuming $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ finite, $n$ a finite index type and $G$ a topological group, for a continuous representation $\rho\colon G\to\mathrm{GL}_n(A)$ the object `TraceAlgebra.obj ρ` is this construction applied to $\mathrm{traceSubalgebra}\,\mathcal O\,\rho$, the topological closure of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the traces $\operatorname{tr}\rho(g)$, $g\in G$; `TraceAlgebra.ι ρ` is its inclusion into $A$.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib provides `Subalgebra.topologicalClosure` and the local-ring and linear-topology API used here; the category `ProartinianCat`, the classes `IsLocalProartinianAlgebra`, [`IsProartinian`](../def/Deformations_IsProartinian.html#L185) and [`IsResidueAlgebra`](../def/Deformations_IsResidueAlgebra.html#L15), and the statement that a closed subalgebra of a compact object is again such an object are the project's own.
--
--   **Where it is used.** Realising the trace algebra $A^{\mathrm{tr}}_\rho$ as an object of the category of pro-Artinian local $\mathcal O$-algebras, rather than merely as a subring of $A$, is what allows deformations to be descended along the inclusion $A^{\mathrm{tr}}_\rho\hookrightarrow A$ and the deformation functor to be corepresented; the same unit-detection lemma makes equaliser subalgebras objects, so the category has finite limits. These are ingredients of the deformation-theoretic input to the modularity lifting arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_Deformations_ClosedSubalgebra.lean

